-- #792 SECOND SHAPE, found by adversarial review of the first fix (#1114) and one token
-- away from its sibling `reject_792_parametric_impl_ground_missing.mdk`: the missing
-- instance is needed at a FUNCTION type rather than at a nullary constructor.
--
-- `debug bumper` needs `Debug (Int -> Int)`. Nothing about that predicate is abstract and
-- no instance can ever match an arrow, so DICT-SEMANTICS §4.2 OD1 makes it a check-time
-- reject — it is OD1's "structurally refutable" population, which is decidable WITHOUT
-- being ground.
--
-- WHY THIS FIXTURE EXISTS SEPARATELY: #1114's first cut filtered the parametric-impl
-- window on `allConcreteHeads`, and `headTyconNameMono` enumerates `TCon`/`TRigid` only —
-- so a fully concrete arrow read as NON-concrete, the window dropped the predicate, and
-- OD4's impl-channel exemption meant no ambiguity fired either. `check` exited 0 while
-- `run` gave `intToString: not an Int` and `build` gave `arg-tag dispatch on impl type
-- that owns no constructors` — #792's own three-verdict signature, restored by a type
-- change its sibling fixture cannot express. A corpus that pins only the `debug Bar`
-- shape reports this as fixed.
data Bar = Bar

interface Foo a where
  foo : a -> String

bumper : Int -> Int
bumper n = n + 1

impl Foo (List a) where
  foo _ = debug bumper

main = println (foo ([1] : List Int))
